                }
            ],
            "product_type": "literature",
            "titles": {
                "en": "‘Since the collar is stiff, no one will feel a small sewn-in note’: Secret Notes from Austrian Resistance Members in Gestapo Captivity"
            },
            "abstracts": {
                "en": "Elfriede Hartmann was 21 years old and a leading member of the Communist Youth League when she was arrested by the Gestapo in Vienna on 24 February 1942. Accused of producing and distributing ‘anti-State propaganda’ and preparing ‘acts of sabotage’, she was held in custody until trial on 22 September 1943, when she was sentenced to death."
            },
